  message: "Deprioritized to P4. This is a Tier 2 IO analysis enhancement requiring type-aware matching (receiver type resolution). The false positives inflate chain counts but don't produce incorrect boundary TYPE classification. Confirmed across the full security-claims curriculum (5 cohorts, 17 repos): affects all Go repos but does not cause FAIL verdicts. The bakeoff assessment scores (mean ~60) are driven primarily by Go interface dispatch and C call edge gaps, not by IO false positives."  # 94f5
